\taxon{Remark}
\title{Algebraic extension versus topological cover}

\p{The extensions in \ref{fcap-001D} and \ref{fcap-001F} are exact
sequences of abstract groups. They record a surjective homomorphism and
its two-element kernel, but no topology. For the positive real form, the
actual finite-dimensional carrier topology, compact double cover, and
connectedness are established in \ref{fcap-0039}; the
stabilizer argument and the universal-cover boundary are established in
\ref{fcap-003A}. Those results do not extend the compact
connectedness conclusion to arbitrary real signature.}
